1. Open Wireshark.
2. Select your active Wi-Fi interface.
3. Double-click the interface to start capture.
4. Open YouTube in browser.
5. Play any video for 20–30 seconds.
6. Return to Wireshark.
7. Click the red Stop button.

DISPLAY FILTERS:
dns
udp
quic
tls
tcp

8. Enter dns in filter bar > press Enter.
9. Observe DNS requests.
10. Enter quic > press Enter.
11. Observe QUIC packets, if present.
12. Enter tls > press Enter.
13. Observe encrypted TLS traffic.
14. Select a packet.
15. Expand packet details in lower panel.

GRAPHS:
16. Click Statistics > I/O Graphs.
17. Observe traffic graph.

OUTPUT:
- Source IP
- Destination IP
- Protocol
- Packet length
- Time
- DNS requests

NOTE:
- If QUIC is not visible, use tls or tcp.
- HTTPS content is encrypted.
- Not every packet captured is necessarily from YouTube.
